{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q019_stable_periodic_release_semantics","answer":"The current-release endpoint (/api/v1/releases/current, also shown in the service index) reports current release version 2.08. Its stable_label is "2.08-stable". Its latest_periodic_update is version "2.08-2026-08-16", dated 2026-08-16. Other reported metadata: SCOPe, public, is_comprehensive false, freeze date 2021-07-28, release date 2021-09-22.

For a reproducible analysis, cite the stable release: 2.08 (label 2.08-stable). Pass release=2.08 explicitly to every call. Do not rely on an unpinned "current" request, because the current pointer can move. Do not cite the periodic label as the base release.

The periodic label, 2.08-2026-08-16, names a dated periodic update built on top of stable release 2.08. It is a date-stamped interim update between stable releases, and it does not replace the stable release. The current-release response gives only the label and date. It does not say which records the update added or changed, or whether any classification changed. I did not verify those details, and the contents of that update are not established by the data I retrieved. To cite a periodic update, quote its full label (2.08-2026-08-16) alongside the stable base 2.08. To confirm what it contains, you would need to query the release-specific endpoints or compare responses from the releases involved.","evidence_used":["scop-homology/SKILL.md","scop-homology/references/api-usage.md","mcp__scope__get_scop_service_info","/api/v1/","/api/v1/releases/current"]}]}
